              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रतिष्ठते — pratiṣṭhate — \"starts on a journey; sets out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यात्रिकः प्रातः गृहात् प्रतिष्ठते। yātrikaḥ prātaḥ gṛhāt pratiṣṭhate. The pilgrim sets out from home in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः प्रातः प्रस्थितवान्, saḥ prātaḥ prasthitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रतिष्ठते (pratiṣṭhate) is built from the prefix pra, \"forth\", and the root √sthā, \"to stand\", which also gives tiṣṭhati, \"stands\"; MW gives pra-sthā as to set out or depart, with the past participle prasthita, and Pāṇini (1.3.22) gives √sthā the middle endings after pra (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
